profile.GENTLE=Gentle
profile.NIL=Nil
profile.HEISENBERG=Heisenberg
profile.GRID=Grid Diagnostic

option.NIL_SCALE=Nil length scale
comment.NIL_SCALE=Controls the pitch of vertical fibers and the strength of area holonomy. Smaller values distort faster.
option.WARP_STRENGTH=Geometry warp
comment.WARP_STRENGTH=Blends Euclidean geometry with the complete Nil transform.
option.FIBER_TWIST=Fiber twist
comment.FIBER_TWIST=Rotates and contracts horizontal layers as their relative height changes.
option.AREA_SHEAR=Area shear
comment.AREA_SHEAR=Raises opposite horizontal sectors according to the Heisenberg central cross term.
option.GROUP_COUPLING=Camera group coupling
comment.GROUP_COUPLING=Uses a smoothly bounded camera inverse term so changing X/Z position shears the vertical fiber without far-coordinate cliffs.
option.FIBER_LIMIT=Fiber shift limit
comment.FIBER_LIMIT=Limits distant vertical displacement in multiples of the Nil length scale.
option.AXIS_ROTATION=Gauge rotation
comment.AXIS_ROTATION=Rotates the two horizontal directions used to expose signed area holonomy.
option.FIBER_TINT=Fiber tint
comment.FIBER_TINT=Colors opposite holonomy sectors cyan and violet.
option.HOLONOMY_GLOW=Holonomy glow
comment.HOLONOMY_GLOW=Adds subtle helical highlights around the vertical fiber.
option.DISTANCE_FOG=Distance fog
comment.DISTANCE_FOG=Fades densely sheared geometry into a dark violet fog.
option.GRID_MODE=Grid mode
comment.GRID_MODE=Draws an orientation-colored coordinate grid on terrain and water before Nil deformation.
value.GRID_MODE.0=Off
value.GRID_MODE.1=Overlay
value.GRID_MODE.2=Diagnostic
option.GRID_SPACING=Grid spacing
comment.GRID_SPACING=Distance in blocks between minor grid lines.
option.GRID_THICKNESS=Grid thickness
comment.GRID_THICKNESS=Screen-space antialiased line thickness multiplier.
option.GRID_OPACITY=Grid opacity
comment.GRID_OPACITY=Controls the strength of minor and major grid lines.
option.GRID_MAJOR_EVERY=Major interval
comment.GRID_MAJOR_EVERY=Draws a bright major line after this many minor cells.
